Round 10 (2026-02-26)

What changed this round (landed)
- Landed code changes in:
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
- Two runtime-side improvements:
  1) Added depth accounting/guard to `aot_try_call`:
     - New limit `AOT_TRY_CALL_MAX_DEPTH=1024`.
     - `aot_try_call` now checks depth cap and increments/decrements `AOT_CALL_DEPTH`
       around direct compiled calls from `wnf` REF dispatch.
     - This closes a latent safety hole where `aot_try_call` previously bypassed
       depth tracking used by `aot_call_ref`.
  2) Split fallback telemetry into true deopts vs intentional residualization:
     - New residual counters for reasons/sites/overflow.
     - `aot_deopt_reason_is_residual()` classifies:
       - `EXPR_APP_ARG_CAPTURE`
       - `EXPR_OP2_RHS_CAPTURE`
     - `aot_deopt_dump()` now prints both streams:
       - `AOT_DEOPT ...` (hard bailouts/mismatches)
       - `AOT_RESID ...` (planned lazy captures)
     - Top-site reporting and reason breakdown preserved for both streams.

Important failed attempt (reverted before landing)
- I temporarily re-enabled compiled REF calls inside `aot_force_whnf_local`
  (removed local `AOT_TRY_CALL_ENABLED=0` gate), using only depth bounds.
- Result: deopt explosion on strict MAT mismatch sites:
  - `gab_tak`: deopt total jumped to `2840`
  - `gab_takl`: deopt total jumped to `8,349,770`
  - dominant reason: `EXPR_UNSUPPORTED_TAG` at `HEAD_MAT_NON_CTR` strict sites.
- Although correctness stayed intact, telemetry quality regressed badly and this is not
  a stable path yet. I restored the force-local gate.

