Operational notes
- `--as-c` artifact path remains deterministic; keep parity/deopt probes serial.
- Force-local compiled REF re-entry remains disabled for now; depth-only re-enable
  is not sufficient with current strict MAT handling.

Lessons
- Deopt counters were mixing two different phenomena (bailout vs planned laziness).
  Splitting them makes hotspot triage reliable again.
- Re-enabling compiled calls inside local WHNF force requires an explicit semantic
  contract for strict mismatch continuation, not just depth limits.

Next likely steps
- Investigate the remaining singleton `EXPR_APP_UNSUPPORTED_FUN` site (now isolated as
  the only true deopt in `gab_tak*`) and classify safe emission rule(s).
- Keep force-local REF policy conservative until a bounded contract/trampoline design
  is specified and proven on `match_recursive_arg`-style recursion.
- Run `HVM_AOT_DEOPT=1` across broader admission benches using the new split stream to
  identify top true deopts (not residual captures).
